# What `docker build .` must NOT send to the builder (Phase 7 B1, D-064).
# The image needs only: src/, web/ (to build the UI), requirements-server.txt, Dockerfile.
# Everything else stays on the laptop: secrets, data, caches, tools, notes.

# --- secrets: NEVER in an image (an image pushed to a registry can be downloaded) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- local environments and caches (rebuilt inside the image) ---
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.cache/
hf_cache/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# --- data and indexes (the server gets its own: volumes + the snapshot seed, B4) ---
data/
qdrant_local/
qdrant_storage/
*.db
*.sqlite
mlflow.db
mlruns/
mlartifacts/

# --- not needed to RUN the app ---
.git/
.github/
docs/
evals/
labs/
tests/
ui/
scripts/
docker/
infra/
deploy/
*.md
!README.md
